# Apollo Builders — edge routing rules for static SPA hosts that respect
# the Netlify-style `_redirects` convention (Netlify, Cloudflare Pages,
# Render, etc). Purpose: return REAL HTTP 404 for unknown routes while
# still serving React Router index.html (200) for known routes.
#
# Behaviour:
#   • Physical files under /images, /static, /robots.txt, /sitemap.xml,
#     etc are served directly (200) — _redirects only applies when no
#     file matches the request path.
#   • Every canonical SPA route below is rewritten to /index.html with
#     a 200 status so React Router can render the correct page.
#   • Anything else falls through the final wildcard and is served as
#     /404.html with a real HTTP 404 status.
#
# If the deployment edge does NOT respect this file, it is harmless —
# the CRA build ignores it and the React SPA still handles unknown
# routes client-side via the NotFound page (noindex, nofollow).

